{
	title: 'Session ids: Hal days from 05:00 and hourly words',
	spec: "Session ids are '<day>-<word>' and list in roughly creation order. A Hal day runs from 05:00 to 05:00 local time; both the day number and the hour slots follow it, so a session at 04:30 gets a late word (zoo) and one at 05:30 the next day's number and an early word (abc). Daylight saving time is ignored. state/epoch.ason holds the home's first session's UTC time ({ epoch: '<ISO>' }), written by that session. day: 1 for the Hal day containing the epoch (a first session at 03:00 local belongs to the Hal day that began the previous 05:00), +1 at each later 05:00 local, padded to two digits; so everyone's first session is 01-<word> and the next 05:00 starts 02. A home continuing old Hal's sessions stores old Hal's epoch (2026-04-24T10:09:20.287Z). word: three lowercase letters from session-words.txt, this task's artifact (sorted, deduplicated; crude and charged words removed), which src/host/session-words.txt copies verbatim. The list is cut into 24 equal slots, slot 0 for 05-06 and slot 23 for 04-05. Tries: 3 from the current slot, 2 from it and its neighbours (not wrapping across 05:00), 5 from the whole list, then random letters until one is free; the directory is claimed by non-recursive mkdir. An invalid epoch file throws. No tests for the id choice.",
	status: 'done',
	needs: [],
	foldInto: ['pe']
}
